WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.163
Why this chapter?

2
00:00:01.163 --> 00:00:04.059
Message center is where
Microsoft tells a tenant

3
00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:07.025
about retirements and
changes, often months ahead.

4
00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:08.939
But a post that nobody reads,

5
00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:12.850
or that only arrives by email,
doesn't become anyone's task.

6
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.600
So the goal is precise.

7
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:19.199
By the end you can read a tenant's Message
center posts and service health issues

8
00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:23.381
with just two read permissions, on the
host for the tenant's own cloud, into

9
00:00:23.381 --> 00:00:28.050
records that say which posts need action
and whether Microsoft or the kit said so.

10
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:32.098
This is for the developers, the
Microsoft 365 service owner,

11
00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:35.300
and the change manager
who receives the tasks.
